  "question": {
    "text": "In thermodynamics, heat and work are :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Path functions",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Intensive thermodynamic state variables",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Extensive thermodynamic state variables",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Point functions",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Heat and work are treated as path functions in thermodynamics.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>W</mi></math></p><p>Since work done by gas depends on type of process i.e. path and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi></math>&nbsp;depends just on initial and final states, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> i.e. heat, also has to depend on process is path.</p>"
  }
